WEBVTT

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:59.410
to have their passports on hand at the gate.

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:14.380
Knock off 50 drachmas and we'll talk.

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:16.640
That doesn't look 8th century to me, pal.

00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:17.940
A wise decision.

00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:20.040
That's hardly even 10th century.

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:22.900
Virgil, Norman, hey, what up?

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:23.800
What are you guys doing here?

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:26.820
I had a sudden imminent feeling that you were in need of help.

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:29.310
I know you're on vacation, but, um...

00:02:29.310 --> 00:02:30.000
Perfect timing.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:34.800
Virgil, you've been around. Come take a look at the ceramic vase in the shop. I can't decide.

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:38.140
And could you hold my Jadaberry oil, please, Max? We'll be right back.

00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:39.190
Okay, Mom.

00:02:39.190 --> 00:02:44.050
Oh, way!

00:02:44.050 --> 00:02:46.510
Yeah, this will keep the bugs from biting all right.

00:02:46.510 --> 00:02:49.890
Turkish furniture polish. Great, Mom.

00:02:49.890 --> 00:02:59.190
Hey, big man. Come see. I have good deal for you.

00:03:00.190 --> 00:03:04.100
No thanks, I already got one.

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:12.080
Hey, get a load of these!

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:15.040
Swell, made in America.

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:17.090
I come all the way to Turkey for this?

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:35.960
Him, him! He stole my hat!

00:03:35.960 --> 00:03:38.740
Uh, sorry mister, this hat's mine. Case closed.

00:03:38.740 --> 00:03:40.980
Police! Steve! Stop that boy!

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:43.260
*Gasp*

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:44.730
Passport.

00:03:44.730 --> 00:03:46.070
My passport?

00:03:46.070 --> 00:03:49.400
Oh, yeah, my mom has it. You guys sit tight, I'll be right back.

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:51.790
Hey!

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:04.130
*laughs*

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:48.430
Don't do it, Norman!

00:04:48.430 --> 00:04:50.430
Great! Where did Max and Norman go?

00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:54.990
There's really no telling.

00:04:54.990 --> 00:05:00.000
Excuse me, has anyone seen a big man with a sword and a young American?

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:08.620
boy wearing a cap they were here a moment ago thieves i tell you both of them boy tried to steal

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:14.520
cap but police come and make boy give back to me then big man attack police they have no passport

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:20.090
and soldiers take them away what my son tried to steal a cap and got arrested where did the

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:29.830
soldiers take them wait where is the cap now

00:05:30.860 --> 00:05:31.860
I sell it already.

00:05:31.860 --> 00:05:32.850
Sold it!

00:05:32.850 --> 00:05:33.970
Got plenty more.

00:05:33.970 --> 00:05:36.000
Only $20 US.

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:37.190
See it! Up there!

00:05:37.190 --> 00:05:39.170
Some kid on a bicycle's wearing it!

00:05:39.170 --> 00:05:42.130
Come on, we've got to get the Mighty One's cap back.

00:05:42.130 --> 00:05:45.080
We've got to get Max first.

00:05:45.080 --> 00:05:50.030
Who's to say that we can even get them out of that place unless we use the cap to open a portal?

00:05:50.030 --> 00:05:55.030
Norman will protect Max, but please let us make haste to find the cap while we still can.

00:05:55.030 --> 00:05:58.260
Why, without it, we might all be doomed.

00:06:00.090 --> 00:06:02.350
- Oh, all right, the hat first.

00:06:02.350 --> 00:06:05.730
But so help me, Virgil, if anything happens to my Max,

00:06:05.730 --> 00:06:07.400
I'll wring your chicken neck.

00:06:32.460 --> 00:06:43.380
hope the guy wearing these got off for good behavior if they hadn't taken my

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:47.910
sword I'd get through well maybe but that's swords police property now normie

00:06:47.910 --> 00:06:52.230
oh yeah I'm glad you didn't attack him with it we'd really be in trouble you see

00:06:52.230 --> 00:06:57.550
major force isn't always the best way I'm the guardian it's what I do well when

00:06:57.550 --> 00:07:00.000
you're outnumbered like that sometimes the best thing to do is just

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:01.260
Just smile and nod.

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:03.480
I don't mind being outnumbered.

00:07:03.720 --> 00:07:04.000
Oh no?

00:07:04.240 --> 00:07:06.540
Do you mind being locked up in a Turkish prison for the rest of your life?

00:07:07.030 --> 00:07:09.470
Norman, just listen to me from now on when I say stop.

00:07:09.510 --> 00:07:10.070
Okie dokie?

00:07:10.640 --> 00:07:12.740
Okie dokie, mighty one.

00:07:16.530 --> 00:07:19.390
Wait, wait, wait!

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:21.030
Don't I get to make my one phone call?

00:07:21.350 --> 00:07:23.670
My mom will be worried if I don't call her and let her know I'm in jail.

00:07:24.900 --> 00:07:25.140
Ew.

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:27.960
Maybe I should just consider ordering a pizza instead, huh?

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:29.920
Ha ha ha ha ha!

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:34.130
You think this is America, hey, little boy?

00:07:34.610 --> 00:07:35.050
Ouch!

00:07:37.140 --> 00:07:39.750
You can stop, Norman.

00:07:39.910 --> 00:07:41.370
I think I heard him say sorry.

00:07:42.330 --> 00:07:43.310
Excellent, Norman.

00:07:43.630 --> 00:07:45.530
You listened to me this time very good.

00:07:46.450 --> 00:07:48.380
Don't worry, little boy.

00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:51.420
You and your big friend will not be here too much longer.

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:56.040
You know, it's funny, but getting out of here really doesn't seem like a big threat to me.

00:07:59.550 --> 00:08:00.000
Well, I haven't.

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:02.120
time to stay for tea anyway, thank you.

00:08:02.120 --> 00:08:12.810
Good evening, ma'am. Uh, perhaps

00:08:12.810 --> 00:08:15.050
you can help. I'm looking for

00:08:15.050 --> 00:08:17.050
a little boy with this hat

00:08:17.050 --> 00:08:23.190
and a bicycle.

00:08:23.190 --> 00:08:26.650
Oh, no, I...

00:08:26.650 --> 00:08:28.070
...should really brush up on my Turkish.

00:08:30.220 --> 00:08:31.890
Teach me some Turkish, quick!

00:08:31.890 --> 00:08:38.930
The particular dialect I learned went out of fashion about the same time my beak became passé, I'm afraid.

00:09:39.920 --> 00:09:40.560
Are you okay, buddy?

00:09:47.340 --> 00:09:48.090
Help!

00:09:48.530 --> 00:09:51.940
There's a huge guy in here trying to kill us!

00:09:53.170 --> 00:09:54.290
Where'd he go?

00:09:54.860 --> 00:09:56.260
Did you see how he got out of here, Norman?

00:09:56.730 --> 00:09:58.280
Dripped out the drain.

00:09:58.610 --> 00:10:00.000
If I had my sword.

00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:07.180
Well, okay, he was huge, and he had a crooked head with hair on his face, like this.

00:10:09.740 --> 00:10:12.120
Torlach, he come to clean the prison.

00:10:13.280 --> 00:10:16.300
Glad he left his mop at home.

00:10:17.280 --> 00:10:20.200
Hey, pal, if that guy's the janitor, I'm the Dalai Lama.

00:10:20.570 --> 00:10:22.790
No escape from Torlach the Torture.

00:10:23.560 --> 00:10:27.440
Oh, your young flesh will make Cyclops fine meal.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:31.400
Cyclops?

00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:33.300
Cyclops cave below.

00:10:33.300 --> 00:10:34.980
You know Odysseus?

00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:38.020
Torturer one of Odysseus' men left behind.

00:10:38.020 --> 00:10:40.320
Now he feeds Cyclops.

00:10:40.320 --> 00:10:41.860
Well, hold on, time out.

00:10:41.860 --> 00:10:44.570
We're losing a little something in the translation here, bud.

00:10:44.570 --> 00:10:47.790
Or you're taking your Greek myths a little too seriously.

00:10:47.790 --> 00:10:51.930
Ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha.

00:10:51.930 --> 00:10:53.760
Applesauce.

00:10:53.760 --> 00:10:57.480
Man, if Odysseus really slept here, you'd think they'd make it more of a tourist attraction.

00:10:57.480 --> 00:11:00.000
But that don't explain how that torturer dude got out of here.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:02.560
If we knew that, maybe we could blow this taco stand, too.

00:11:06.220 --> 00:11:08.760
I got blisters on my knuckles from all this knocking.

00:11:09.510 --> 00:11:13.780
Sit, Virgil. We've left Max sitting in some jail all night. We're going to get him out.

00:11:14.370 --> 00:11:16.270
Forget the hat. My son's more important.

00:11:18.920 --> 00:11:22.880
Ah! Watch where... That's him! Stop you! Hey!

00:11:27.520 --> 00:11:29.840
Hey, not touch my bike!

00:11:30.060 --> 00:11:32.800
Young man, it's very important that I have that cap you're wearing.

00:11:33.080 --> 00:11:34.020
What will you take for it?

00:11:34.260 --> 00:11:36.060
My cap you not have! Let me go my bike!

00:11:36.240 --> 00:11:37.800
I'll buy that cap from you.

00:11:38.020 --> 00:11:40.160
Here, now it's a generous offer on my part.

00:11:40.780 --> 00:11:44.260
Come back here! You're tampering with the fate of the cosmos!

00:11:45.560 --> 00:11:51.850
Excuse me, but my kingdom for a horse!

00:12:14.910 --> 00:12:20.160
minute while i get right side up oh dear a pork club

00:12:34.860 --> 00:12:35.520
I'm not sure.

00:12:37.940 --> 00:12:43.130
Wait a moment, please.

00:12:44.030 --> 00:12:52.600
I'm not mistaken, this is the scenic Serengeti plane, and these charming beasts saw...

00:12:52.600 --> 00:12:54.470
Killer baboons!

00:12:55.800 --> 00:12:59.890
Monkey!

00:13:07.770 --> 00:13:26.780
And I hit them and hit the bike.

00:13:26.780 --> 00:13:30.000
Come on, he couldn't have passed through a solid wall.

00:13:30.990 --> 00:13:34.970
maybe there's some kind of hidden door but where look there is a door arrow

00:13:34.970 --> 00:13:55.730
leaked through from the other side allow me he lucky a map now if nobody's done

00:13:55.730 --> 00:13:59.200
any remodeling of this place since this map was carved then this main corridor

00:13:59.200 --> 00:14:00.000
will lead us straight out

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:11.200
Hey, this must be the Cyclops that Nutball Guard was telling us about, huh?

00:14:11.200 --> 00:14:15.990
It's times like these when I really miss that old sword of yours, Normie.

00:14:15.990 --> 00:14:18.490
I don't have anything to pick that padlock with, though.

00:14:18.490 --> 00:14:19.490
I do.

00:14:19.490 --> 00:14:29.160
Whoever lives here has got to be...

00:14:31.790 --> 00:14:37.160
I'm dead!

00:14:37.160 --> 00:14:38.210
Jeez!

00:14:38.210 --> 00:14:40.060
This place reeks big time!

00:14:40.060 --> 00:14:42.060
Smells like rotten Easter eggs getting a perm!

00:14:42.060 --> 00:14:46.950
Yeah, it's worse, Norm.

00:14:46.950 --> 00:14:48.720
I think we're in the prison sewer!

00:15:06.560 --> 00:15:07.740
Please let this be an exit.

00:15:22.980 --> 00:15:30.000
Good luck, Normie.

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:43.760
I think our bell's going to lend us an axe!

00:16:31.020 --> 00:16:57.810
This dude must have had a lot of trouble finding clothes in his size.

00:17:02.650 --> 00:17:04.440
Looks like he ate a rummage sale!

00:17:04.440 --> 00:17:06.530
Mom would go nuts!

00:17:06.530 --> 00:17:11.630
Cool!

00:17:11.630 --> 00:17:16.110
Norman, look above the skull!

00:17:16.110 --> 00:17:16.900
Let's go!

00:17:33.000 --> 00:17:34.230
It is an exit!

00:17:34.230 --> 00:17:47.040
What's that?

00:17:47.040 --> 00:17:53.400
Teamverse.

00:18:04.920 --> 00:18:06.690
Slugging tentacle off me!

00:19:09.630 --> 00:19:11.390
Yeah, yeah, this would have been easy.

00:19:11.750 --> 00:19:15.200
If we'd used a latch to open the door, this would have been...

00:19:15.200 --> 00:19:19.470
Oh, what kind of self-respecting secret passageway would lead into a prison yard?

00:19:19.990 --> 00:19:21.550
Ah, there you are.

00:19:23.040 --> 00:19:24.830
We look all over for you.

00:19:25.190 --> 00:19:28.930
Lady, bring your passport, so it's fine for you to go now.

00:19:31.370 --> 00:19:34.260
Oh, are you guys a sight for sore eyeballs?

00:19:34.260 --> 00:19:37.750
Boy, you will never guess what happened to us!

00:20:13.340 --> 00:20:15.660
Planning about not having your sword, you didn't even use it?

00:20:16.130 --> 00:20:18.140
Why do you even bother with it, Normie?

00:20:18.800 --> 00:20:20.060
I like it.

00:20:20.650 --> 00:20:22.360
Max, what did you do with my jettaberry oil?

00:20:22.990 --> 00:20:25.990
Um, I sort of gave a guy a burning case of pink eye.

00:20:26.650 --> 00:20:28.780
And how'd you manage to melt your sneaker?

00:20:29.040 --> 00:20:30.000
You have to be more careful.

00:20:30.030 --> 00:20:32.530
Well, you know, that's the third pair you've ruined this month.

00:20:32.530 --> 00:20:34.630
And you look hungry. When did you eat last?

00:20:34.630 --> 00:20:36.630
Oh, quick, Virgil, where's the nearest portal?

00:20:36.630 --> 00:20:45.120
I don't care where it goes, just get me out of here, man.

00:20:45.120 --> 00:20:50.390
This week, we went to the ancient land of Turkey,

00:20:50.390 --> 00:20:54.600
where people have lived in cities dating as far back as 7700 B.C.

00:20:54.600 --> 00:20:57.300
Archaeologists like Schliemann, Derbfeld, and Blagen

00:20:57.300 --> 00:21:00.000
have uncovered buildings built on top of other buildings,

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:02.020
along with some of the treasures of ancient history.

00:21:02.540 --> 00:21:04.960
Right now, I'd like to uncover a cheeseburger, fries, and a soda.

00:21:05.320 --> 00:21:05.980
See you next week.
